{ This file is generated by the Clifford toolkit (clgencore.pas).
  Do not edit it by hand: change the generator and regenerate instead.

  Signature: 3 basis vectors square to +1, 0 to -1.

  Conventions:
  - Dot is the "fat" dot product: e_A . e_B = e_A e_B when one index set
    contains the other, 0 otherwise (scalars included).
  - Involute is the grade involution, Conjugate the Clifford conjugate.
  - SquaredNorm is <X ~X>_0; Norm is Sqrt(Abs(SquaredNorm)).
  - Dual is X * I, with I the unit pseudoscalar.
  - Inverse is the multiplicative inverse (left and right inverses coincide);
    dividing by a non-invertible value raises a floating-point exception.
  - X.Rotation(A, B) is B A X A^-1 B^-1: the composition of two reflections,
    i.e. a rotation in the plane A^B by TWICE the angle from A to B.
  - X.Rotate(R) is R X ~R, for a rotor R with R ~R = 1; it keeps the type
    of X and drops the components of other grades.
}

